1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:02,010
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,070 --> 00:00:03,310
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:05,080
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:08,850
Was Eun Seol the one
who leaked the story about her?

5
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:11,480
No.

6
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:13,520
No?

7
00:00:14,390 --> 00:00:16,590
That's right. Eun Seol didn't do it.

8
00:00:17,090 --> 00:00:18,090
How do you know that?

9
00:00:19,490 --> 00:00:21,030
How do you know that it wasn't her?

10
00:00:22,930 --> 00:00:24,930
Because Eun Seol said it wasn't her.

11
00:00:26,870 --> 00:00:27,870
Then...

12
00:00:39,310 --> 00:00:41,650
Ms. Kang, aren't you heading home?

13
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:43,680
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

14
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:45,380
Is it that late already?

15
00:00:48,450 --> 00:00:49,650
Ms. Ko, aren't you calling it a day?

16
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:53,630
Go on ahead.

17
00:00:54,290 --> 00:00:55,460
I have to work overtime.

18
00:00:57,130 --> 00:00:59,330
All right. Good luck with your work.

19
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:13,610
(2024 Product Review 015)

20
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:18,750
Is that a file number?

21
00:01:20,890 --> 00:01:23,490
(Integrated Search:
2024 Product Review 015)

22
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:24,860
(2024 Product Review 015
by Lee Young Ung)

23
00:01:25,690 --> 00:01:26,690
What the...

24
00:01:27,230 --> 00:01:28,460
It's all been entered already.

25
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:34,430
All I had to do was compile it?

26
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:41,870
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

27
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:43,070
Seok Jin, let's head home.

28
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:45,580
I have to work late,
so you go on ahead.

29
00:01:46,010 --> 00:01:47,050
You're working late too?

30
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:48,880
Who else is staying late?

31
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:52,250
No one.

32
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:53,850
Honestly.

33
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:57,990
Then I'll just stay here
and watch you work.

34
00:02:00,530 --> 00:02:03,830
Kang Hae Ra, you're distracting me.
Go home first.

35
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:06,830
I won't be a distraction.
Just pretend I'm not here.

36
00:02:40,270 --> 00:02:41,770
(Manager Park Seong Min)

37
00:02:51,410 --> 00:02:52,410
(Enter Password)

38
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:58,380
(Manager Park Seong Min)

39
00:03:04,690 --> 00:03:08,360
"Two o'clock,
visit the Anseong Plant."

40
00:03:28,610 --> 00:03:29,950
Manager Park, are you still here?

41
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:33,720
Seriously?

42
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:36,050
Did he really just go home
with the lights on?

43
00:03:58,140 --> 00:03:59,140
Who's there?

44
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:02,450
Goodness, Ms. Kang.

45
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:04,820
What are you doing here?

46
00:04:05,550 --> 00:04:07,120
The lights were on,
so I thought you were working late.

47
00:04:07,350 --> 00:04:08,350
The lights?

48
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:11,620
Did I forget to turn them off?

49
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:13,220
Why did you come back?

50
00:04:13,390 --> 00:04:14,590
I left my phone.

51
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:16,360
My phone...

52
00:04:18,130 --> 00:04:19,860
Where's my phone?

53
00:04:25,570 --> 00:04:29,140
I'm sorry to ask,
but could you call my phone?

54
00:04:32,210 --> 00:04:33,980
Seriously, where's your head at?

55
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:52,600
And turn off the lights.
It's all company money.

56
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:54,630
Of course. Shall we?

57
00:05:05,810 --> 00:05:08,410
(Manager Park Seong Min)

58
00:05:54,030 --> 00:05:55,290
Working late?

59
00:05:56,130 --> 00:05:57,130
Yes.

60
00:05:57,730 --> 00:06:00,700
You gave the new hire so much work
she's staying late?

61
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:04,100
You think it's the workload?
She's just inexperienced.

62
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:06,340
Isn't that right, Ms. Ko?

63
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:08,470
Yes, that's right.

64
00:06:08,770 --> 00:06:09,970
I haven't gotten the hang of it yet.

65
00:06:12,110 --> 00:06:14,310
Well, I'll be going now.

66
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:25,520
You're working late too?

67
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:27,430
Who else is staying late?

68
00:06:29,590 --> 00:06:30,630
No one.

69
00:06:30,630 --> 00:06:31,630
What's wrong, Seok Jin?

70
00:06:38,070 --> 00:06:39,070
Hae Ra.

71
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:44,040
I hope you don't do anything
to disappoint me.

72
00:06:45,610 --> 00:06:47,010
You know what I mean, right?

73
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:52,150
Let's go.

74
00:06:55,590 --> 00:06:57,460
That was extremely risky.

75
00:06:57,860 --> 00:06:58,960
Tell me about it.

76
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:02,260
So can we eliminate
the Sales Manager...

77
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:04,430
and Logistics Manager as suspects?

78
00:07:04,730 --> 00:07:05,830
Not yet.

79
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:07,370
Why not?

80
00:07:07,630 --> 00:07:10,030
You said you confirmed
their schedules for June 5.

81
00:07:10,770 --> 00:07:12,870
I haven't been able
to cross-check them yet.

82
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:14,670
Cross-check?

83
00:07:16,210 --> 00:07:17,210
That's true.

84
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:20,550
Okay, then I'll verify
the Sales Manager's...

85
00:07:20,550 --> 00:07:21,650
overseas business trip.

86
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:24,780
As part of the Legal Team,
I can pull up his travel records.

87
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,050
- Really?
- Yes.

88
00:07:28,220 --> 00:07:31,420
But how do we confirm
the Logistics Manager's schedule?

89
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:34,430
I was planning to go
to the Anseong Plant in person.

90
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:36,760
Then I'll go with you.

91
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:38,030
I can go by myself.

92
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:40,000
But you don't have a car.

93
00:07:40,430 --> 00:07:42,770
Besides, I'm free
this weekend anyway,

94
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:44,100
so I'll drive you.

95
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:46,700
Thank you, Attorney Seo.

96
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:48,610
Don't mention it.

97
00:07:49,110 --> 00:07:52,210
Plus, it gives me a chance
to get some fresh air.

98
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:56,880
That reminds me.

99
00:07:58,950 --> 00:08:00,850
There's one thing
that's been bothering me.

100
00:08:01,450 --> 00:08:02,550
What is it?

101
00:08:02,990 --> 00:08:06,990
I had a chance to speak
with Chief Cha earlier,

102
00:08:07,690 --> 00:08:10,930
and he asked
if you were behind the fake news.

103
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:13,970
And?

104
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,730
I told him it wasn't you,

105
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:17,400
but he didn't seem to believe me.

106
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:21,670
Will what I said
get you into trouble?

107
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:27,350
It is what it is, right?

108
00:08:28,510 --> 00:08:29,510
Anyway,

109
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:32,920
you two don't seem like
just friends from school.

110
00:08:33,890 --> 00:08:34,890
Why's that?

111
00:08:35,290 --> 00:08:37,890
No reason.
I just got that impression.

112
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:41,490
That's all in the past now.

113
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:47,630
It seems Director Han
isn't doing well.

114
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:49,200
I'm going to stop by and visit him.

115
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:51,970
So will you be very late?

116
00:08:54,170 --> 00:08:55,340
All right.

117
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:59,380
And please give my regards
to Director Han.

118
00:09:02,550 --> 00:09:04,520
Is CEO Kang running late?

119
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:07,620
Yes. Director Han
has been hospitalized,

120
00:09:07,620 --> 00:09:09,090
so he's going to visit him.

121
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:12,490
By Director Han,
do you mean Director Han Cheol Soo?

122
00:09:12,590 --> 00:09:14,960
He's an old college friend
of Young Hoon's.

123
00:09:15,490 --> 00:09:16,930
He has terminal liver cancer.

124
00:09:16,990 --> 00:09:18,900
They say he won't make it
past this year.

125
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:22,270
Oh my. That's terrible.

126
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:26,170
I know. He's still so young.

127
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:27,840
It's just so tragic.

128
00:09:29,970 --> 00:09:32,510
Well, anyway...

129
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:36,550
I know it sounds insensitive
when someone is so ill,

130
00:09:36,810 --> 00:09:40,120
but you should start thinking
about a replacement director.

131
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:44,760
I know. It seems we'll have to.

132
00:09:45,690 --> 00:09:48,830
Do you have anyone in mind?

133
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:52,900
No, my husband will take care of it.

134
00:09:54,970 --> 00:09:56,730
Don't say that.

135
00:09:57,230 --> 00:09:59,640
You should start taking
a more active role...

136
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:01,040
in the foundation's affairs.

137
00:10:01,910 --> 00:10:02,940
Me?

138
00:10:03,570 --> 00:10:05,540
You couldn't increase
the scholarship budget...

139
00:10:05,610 --> 00:10:08,110
because of the CEO, right?

140
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:10,850
Oh, that?

141
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:13,620
I backed down
because my husband was right.

142
00:10:13,990 --> 00:10:17,250
What will you do if he says
the company is in trouble...

143
00:10:17,250 --> 00:10:20,060
and makes deep cuts
to the scholarship budget?

144
00:10:20,090 --> 00:10:22,530
Come on. He wouldn't.

145
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:27,670
The former chairman cherished
the scholarship foundation.

146
00:10:28,430 --> 00:10:30,700
Why else would he have
entrusted it to you?

147
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,670
That's why you need to be
more proactive.

148
00:10:33,770 --> 00:10:35,340
For Cheongma's sake, at least.

149
00:10:36,570 --> 00:10:40,180
All right.
I'll take your advice to heart.

150
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:45,050
I knew I could count on you
to look out for me, Director Joo.

151
00:10:46,650 --> 00:10:47,690
Anytime.

152
00:10:54,660 --> 00:10:55,660
Wait.

153
00:10:58,460 --> 00:10:59,700
My necklace.

154
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:02,000
Where did my necklace go?

155
00:11:07,610 --> 00:11:09,070
Can I come in for a second?

156
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:11,180
Sure, come in.

157
00:11:18,420 --> 00:11:20,950
How's work? Are you managing okay?

158
00:11:21,390 --> 00:11:22,950
Yes, it's good.

159
00:11:23,490 --> 00:11:25,960
And there are no rumors about you
at the company?

160
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:29,560
Thankfully, it seems the CEO
is keeping a tight lid on it.

161
00:11:31,130 --> 00:11:32,330
That's a relief, at least.

162
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:35,870
Anyway, what's that?

163
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:38,200
This?

164
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:40,440
It's a business plan.

165
00:11:40,910 --> 00:11:42,410
A business plan?

166
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:44,380
You actually drafted one?

167
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:46,180
Hey, I'm doing this
with your hard-earned money,

168
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,710
so I have to be thorough.

169
00:11:48,450 --> 00:11:49,650
I can't let it fail.

170
00:11:51,250 --> 00:11:52,280
Take a look.

171
00:11:52,750 --> 00:11:56,090
See which of these looks promising
and give it some thought.

172
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:59,860
It's not like I'd know
just by looking.

173
00:12:02,190 --> 00:12:05,700
Watching you get into Cheongma
was truly impressive.

174
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:08,130
Honestly, even though
you're my sister,

175
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:10,700
it made me respect you a little.

176
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:13,470
If it were me,

177
00:12:13,470 --> 00:12:15,970
I would've completely fallen apart
long ago.

178
00:12:21,450 --> 00:12:23,210
I've never formally apologized,
have I?

179
00:12:27,790 --> 00:12:29,750
I'm truly sorry.

180
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:33,260
Thank you.

181
00:12:35,390 --> 00:12:36,430
Okay, then.

182
00:12:37,130 --> 00:12:38,330
Look them over...

183
00:12:39,230 --> 00:12:40,630
and let me know later.

184
00:12:41,470 --> 00:12:42,470
I will.

185
00:12:53,540 --> 00:12:55,050
Seo Hyun Jae.

186
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:58,950
Wait, did you have plans
this weekend?

187
00:12:58,950 --> 00:13:00,020
Yes.

188
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:01,520
Where are you going?

189
00:13:01,520 --> 00:13:02,590
I have plans.

190
00:13:03,590 --> 00:13:04,720
What plans?

191
00:13:06,020 --> 00:13:08,590
Am I Teun Teun?
Why do I need to report that to you?

192
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:10,560
How do I look?

193
00:13:11,230 --> 00:13:13,100
- You look fine.
- I'm off.

194
00:13:16,070 --> 00:13:17,130
What's with him?

195
00:13:22,770 --> 00:13:24,810
I confirmed
the Sales Manager's business trip.

196
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:28,110
He was in Shanghai on business
from the 4th to the 8th.

197
00:13:29,110 --> 00:13:30,110
Good.

198
00:13:30,410 --> 00:13:32,380
Then we've eliminated
one more suspect.

199
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:35,590
I found out something else.

200
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:38,720
The General Affairs Manager
doesn't have a driver's license,

201
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:42,930
and the Finance Manager
lost his license to a DUI.

202
00:13:43,390 --> 00:13:45,530
Attorney Seo, no way.

203
00:13:53,870 --> 00:13:55,510
If we go to the factory today...

204
00:13:56,010 --> 00:13:57,370
and check the entry logs,

205
00:13:58,210 --> 00:14:02,280
we should be able to find
who met with Lee Jung Tae that day.

206
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:07,320
But we're showing up
without submitting an official request.

207
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:09,190
Will they still let us
look at the entry logs?

208
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:10,790
Don't worry about that.

209
00:14:11,590 --> 00:14:12,590
Remember,

210
00:14:12,690 --> 00:14:14,730
I'm the Head of Legal
at Cheongma HQ.

211
00:14:16,190 --> 00:14:17,190
Right.

212
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:21,300
And in case there's any trouble,

213
00:14:21,830 --> 00:14:25,140
we'll create a diversion.

214
00:14:51,030 --> 00:14:52,030
Yes?

215
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,230
- Hello.
- Hello.

216
00:14:55,530 --> 00:14:58,700
Hello. We're from Cheongma Group.

217
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,410
I see. What can I do for you?

218
00:15:01,640 --> 00:15:03,810
You keep a log
of all outside vehicles, correct?

219
00:15:04,170 --> 00:15:05,210
We do.

220
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:09,050
Could we possibly take a look
at that log?

221
00:15:11,750 --> 00:15:12,950
What for?

222
00:15:13,050 --> 00:15:16,020
There's something
we need to look into urgently.

223
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:18,260
I'm afraid you can't.

224
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:19,920
It's against regulations
to show it...

225
00:15:19,990 --> 00:15:21,460
to unauthorized personnel.

226
00:15:22,690 --> 00:15:23,690
Oh, right.

227
00:15:25,330 --> 00:15:28,430
I'm the Head of Legal
at Cheongma HQ.

228
00:15:29,430 --> 00:15:31,370
There's something
I absolutely need to confirm.

229
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:33,270
Could you please show it to me?

230
00:15:33,270 --> 00:15:34,540
I really can't.

231
00:15:34,870 --> 00:15:36,910
Even if you're the Head of Legal,

232
00:15:37,210 --> 00:15:40,410
you have to file a formal request
with General Affairs.

233
00:15:41,010 --> 00:15:43,010
Put in an official request
and come back.

234
00:15:57,560 --> 00:15:59,400
Darn. What now?

235
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:02,700
Unbelievable.

236
00:16:15,610 --> 00:16:16,610
Hey.

237
00:16:16,780 --> 00:16:17,980
Hey!

238
00:16:24,690 --> 00:16:25,860
What's the problem?

239
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:27,990
You shouldn't be honking like that.

240
00:16:30,460 --> 00:16:31,900
Wait, me?

241
00:16:32,830 --> 00:16:35,230
My gosh, I'm sorry.

242
00:16:35,230 --> 00:16:37,030
I was listening to music,

243
00:16:37,270 --> 00:16:38,900
so I didn't even realize
I was honking.

244
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:40,740
I'm sorry.

245
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,210
(Vehicle Entry Log)

246
00:16:48,780 --> 00:16:50,310
(Vehicle Entry Log)

247
00:16:54,650 --> 00:16:56,350
Stop loitering and get going.

248
00:16:57,650 --> 00:16:59,020
Right. Sure thing.

249
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:03,660
(Vehicle Entry Log)

250
00:17:03,730 --> 00:17:08,030
(June 5, 2 p.m., 56J 6124,
Logistics Manager Park Seong Min)

251
00:17:22,810 --> 00:17:25,480
Eun Seol, any luck?
Were you able to check?

252
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:28,290
Yes. I confirmed he was here
at 2 p.m. on June 5.

253
00:17:32,690 --> 00:17:34,560
It's beautiful.

254
00:17:35,630 --> 00:17:36,860
Do you like it here?

255
00:17:37,230 --> 00:17:38,230
Yes.

256
00:17:38,300 --> 00:17:40,760
I can't remember the last time
I saw a view like this.

257
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:42,900
Darn.

258
00:17:43,100 --> 00:17:44,670
If I'd known
you'd like it this much,

259
00:17:44,740 --> 00:17:46,170
I would've brought you sooner.

260
00:17:47,470 --> 00:17:50,270
Thank you so much
for bringing me here, Attorney Seo.

261
00:17:51,410 --> 00:17:54,450
Honestly, I haven't been
to a place like this in ages.

262
00:17:54,850 --> 00:17:56,310
- How so?
- Come on.

263
00:17:56,310 --> 00:17:57,850
Who comes to a place
like this alone?

264
00:17:57,920 --> 00:17:59,380
You come with your girlfriend.

265
00:18:00,150 --> 00:18:01,150
I see.

266
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:05,120
I mean, I'm just saying.

267
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:08,230
Aren't you seeing anyone?

268
00:18:08,230 --> 00:18:10,730
Of course not.

269
00:18:13,660 --> 00:18:15,070
Are you ready to order?

270
00:18:15,130 --> 00:18:16,970
Eun Seol,
what would you like to eat?

271
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,270
I'm not familiar
with places like this,

272
00:18:19,270 --> 00:18:20,700
so please order for me.

273
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:22,110
I'm fine with anything.

274
00:18:26,710 --> 00:18:28,280
What do you do best here?

275
00:18:28,780 --> 00:18:31,250
Does your girlfriend
happen to like spicy food?

276
00:18:32,220 --> 00:18:33,280
My...

277
00:18:33,520 --> 00:18:34,820
girlfriend?

278
00:18:35,790 --> 00:18:37,050
We're not together.

279
00:18:37,050 --> 00:18:39,120
Oh, I'm sorry.

280
00:18:39,390 --> 00:18:41,590
It's just that you two look
so good together.

281
00:18:43,630 --> 00:18:45,700
Then we'll have
two servings of this.

282
00:18:45,830 --> 00:18:47,000
Yes, right away.

283
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:48,070
Thank you.

284
00:19:08,790 --> 00:19:10,490
I'm tired.

285
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:14,120
That's why I told you
to just rest at home.

286
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,590
You regret coming along, don't you?

287
00:19:16,560 --> 00:19:19,700
Instead of an amusement park,
a nice drive would've been better.

288
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:22,230
What grown adults go
to amusement parks?

289
00:19:22,330 --> 00:19:24,470
You know my mom's condition,
yet you're still acting this way.

290
00:19:24,970 --> 00:19:27,170
I don't care.
I had a terrible time today,

291
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:28,670
so you owe me one.

292
00:19:29,740 --> 00:19:31,170
What is it that you want?

293
00:19:31,780 --> 00:19:32,780
A kiss.

294
00:19:33,980 --> 00:19:34,980
Hey.

295
00:19:35,450 --> 00:19:36,450
What?

296
00:19:37,210 --> 00:19:39,750
You're being ridiculous.
We're going to get married.

297
00:19:39,950 --> 00:19:41,850
I know, but there's a time
and a place for that.

298
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:43,290
How can we do that here?

299
00:19:44,090 --> 00:19:45,660
Fine. Then I'm sleeping over.

300
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:47,520
What?

301
00:19:50,060 --> 00:19:52,400
Why would you be sleeping over here?

302
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,830
Mom, Hae Ra was just kidding.

303
00:19:59,170 --> 00:20:00,640
I should go wash my hands.

304
00:20:08,110 --> 00:20:09,110
Ms. Park.

305
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:11,010
You don't like me, do you?

306
00:20:11,950 --> 00:20:15,020
That's right. I don't like you.

307
00:20:15,490 --> 00:20:16,490
But why?

308
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:18,720
I even went
to the amusement park with you.

309
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:21,290
Who asked you to come?

310
00:20:21,490 --> 00:20:24,460
I only wanted to go
with Mr. Seok Jin.

311
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:27,660
You're really pushing my buttons.

312
00:20:28,530 --> 00:20:29,530
Ms. Park.

313
00:20:30,430 --> 00:20:32,470
If you keep hating me,

314
00:20:32,870 --> 00:20:34,910
I'm going to take
Seok Jin away from you.

315
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:37,910
What?

316
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:41,480
So get a grip, okay?

317
00:20:42,550 --> 00:20:45,980
Go ahead, try tattling to Seok Jin.
I swear I won't let it slide.

318
00:20:46,550 --> 00:20:47,620
Got it?

319
00:20:49,750 --> 00:20:50,950
Why aren't you answering me?

320
00:20:52,290 --> 00:20:53,890
Should I take Seok Jin from you?

321
00:20:55,090 --> 00:20:57,960
No, please don't. I hear you.

322
00:20:58,030 --> 00:21:00,730
I'll do as you say.

323
00:21:01,330 --> 00:21:03,830
You should've done that
from the start.

324
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:08,370
Let's try to get along, okay?

325
00:21:08,370 --> 00:21:10,570
If you can't, at least fake it.

326
00:21:14,650 --> 00:21:16,380
Mom, you must be hungry.
Let's have dinner.

327
00:21:16,550 --> 00:21:19,280
What? It's okay. I'm fine.

328
00:21:19,420 --> 00:21:22,420
I'm actually tired.
I think I'll go to bed.

329
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:24,760
Okay, then.

330
00:21:28,090 --> 00:21:29,590
She must be really tired.

331
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:31,600
I guess it'll just be
the two of us for dinner.

332
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,000
Let's do that.

333
00:21:37,970 --> 00:21:40,000
I was going to pay for dinner.

334
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:43,010
It doesn't matter who pays
as long as we enjoyed the meal.

335
00:21:43,170 --> 00:21:44,240
You should head inside.

336
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:48,810
Hey, Mi Rae.

337
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:55,050
When you said you had plans,
you meant with Eun Seol?

338
00:21:56,250 --> 00:21:57,320
Yes.

339
00:21:58,120 --> 00:22:00,260
You must be tired.
Go in and get some rest.

340
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:02,530
Sure. You get some rest too,
Attorney Seo.

341
00:22:05,530 --> 00:22:06,630
Good night.

342
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:15,440
So, where did you two go?

343
00:22:16,110 --> 00:22:17,470
We just had some errands to run.

344
00:22:17,770 --> 00:22:19,110
What kind of errands?

345
00:22:19,810 --> 00:22:22,080
I told you, I'm not Teun Teun.

346
00:22:25,150 --> 00:22:26,750
Are you kidding me?

347
00:22:31,320 --> 00:22:32,620
Uncle, did you just get home?

348
00:22:33,190 --> 00:22:34,490
Teun Teun, have you had dinner?

349
00:22:34,690 --> 00:22:36,760
No, not yet. What about you?

350
00:22:37,190 --> 00:22:38,400
I already ate.

351
00:22:38,760 --> 00:22:40,900
You had dinner with Eun Seol too?

352
00:22:42,730 --> 00:22:44,170
Why? Is there a problem with that?

353
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:49,540
I'm warning you.
Stop hanging with Eun Seol...

354
00:22:49,610 --> 00:22:51,040
before people start talking.

355
00:22:52,040 --> 00:22:55,310
- Talk about what?
- You two are always out late.

356
00:22:55,380 --> 00:22:56,780
You think people won't talk?

357
00:22:57,480 --> 00:22:59,020
I don't care.

358
00:23:00,150 --> 00:23:01,280
- Hey.
- Mom.

359
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:02,290
Yes?

360
00:23:02,890 --> 00:23:04,120
Did you buy the soy sauce?

361
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:06,120
The soy sauce!

362
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:09,060
I'll be right back.
Oh, for goodness' sake.

363
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:34,720
(June 5: 12 suspects
with access to company cars)

364
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:36,120
(Sales Manager, Logistics Manager)

365
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:54,770
- Good morning.
- Coffee, Ms. Kang?

366
00:23:56,970 --> 00:23:58,180
Ms. Ko.

367
00:23:58,710 --> 00:24:00,440
Did you finish the data entry
I asked you to do?

368
00:24:01,080 --> 00:24:02,080
Yes.

369
00:24:04,410 --> 00:24:05,680
Are you really saying
you did all of it?

370
00:24:06,550 --> 00:24:09,790
Yes, I uploaded my completed work
to the Design Team's shared folder,

371
00:24:09,790 --> 00:24:10,920
so you can take a look.

372
00:24:12,560 --> 00:24:13,960
Ji Soo, check on it.

373
00:24:14,190 --> 00:24:15,190
Sure.

374
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:23,600
Yes, it's there.

375
00:24:24,730 --> 00:24:27,400
Check it carefully
and make sure it was done properly.

376
00:24:29,070 --> 00:24:30,810
Product review data,

377
00:24:30,910 --> 00:24:33,640
market research reports,
trend analysis by year and brand.

378
00:24:34,210 --> 00:24:35,350
It's all here.

379
00:24:35,850 --> 00:24:37,410
There are 47 files in total.

380
00:24:39,950 --> 00:24:40,980
Really?

381
00:24:42,250 --> 00:24:43,320
Let's dive right into the meeting.

382
00:24:44,550 --> 00:24:45,560
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

383
00:24:52,330 --> 00:24:54,400
Here are the candidates
for the director role you requested.

384
00:24:57,430 --> 00:25:00,300
One's a lawyer,
another runs a talent agency,

385
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:03,240
and the last one
used to be a professor.

386
00:25:04,670 --> 00:25:06,480
Attorney Choi Chang Sik?

387
00:25:07,180 --> 00:25:08,680
You know him well, don't you?

388
00:25:09,180 --> 00:25:10,180
Of course.

389
00:25:10,410 --> 00:25:12,720
He's Chairman Lee's personal lawyer,
so of course I know him.

390
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:14,920
But he's no good.

391
00:25:15,690 --> 00:25:18,490
How so?
I heard he'd do anything for money.

392
00:25:18,960 --> 00:25:21,990
He's just as close to CEO Kang
as he is to Chairman Lee.

393
00:25:22,530 --> 00:25:24,360
Also, there's no guarantee
he'll be completely on my side.

394
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:27,400
Then what about CEO Lee Soo Jin?

395
00:25:28,230 --> 00:25:30,030
I know her inside and out, too.

396
00:25:30,530 --> 00:25:33,040
She managed the agency back
when Chairwoman Lee was an actress.

397
00:25:34,170 --> 00:25:35,210
But she won't work either.

398
00:25:36,110 --> 00:25:38,140
Is she close to CEO Kang as well?

399
00:25:39,340 --> 00:25:40,480
No, but...

400
00:25:41,380 --> 00:25:43,550
She's skilled at sowing discord
and is too perceptive.

401
00:25:44,350 --> 00:25:45,850
She's unsuitable for my purposes.

402
00:25:47,180 --> 00:25:49,490
Then that only leaves
Professor Hong Seok Gyu.

403
00:25:51,290 --> 00:25:52,560
A professor?

404
00:25:53,420 --> 00:25:56,430
Director Han was a professor,
so that's a good thing.

405
00:25:57,930 --> 00:25:59,560
He retired last year?

406
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:03,000
Yes. After retiring,
he had no income,

407
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:04,870
and was just scraping by
on his pension.

408
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:06,800
His son works at a major company,

409
00:26:06,840 --> 00:26:09,010
but he sold his father's house
to cover his gambling debts.

410
00:26:11,740 --> 00:26:13,010
What's his connection
to Chairman Lee?

411
00:26:13,410 --> 00:26:15,510
He's a member
of her calligraphy club.

412
00:26:16,110 --> 00:26:17,110
Is that so?

413
00:26:17,780 --> 00:26:21,950
Then he'll be perfect.
We'll go with him. Set up a meeting.

414
00:26:22,390 --> 00:26:23,390
Got it.

415
00:26:23,720 --> 00:26:27,060
By the way,
what has Ko Eun Seol been up to?

416
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:30,090
There's nothing unusual
to report so far.

417
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:32,560
She's following
Ms. Kang's instructions well.

418
00:26:34,130 --> 00:26:35,200
Keep a closer eye on her.

419
00:26:36,370 --> 00:26:37,370
Understood.

420
00:26:45,380 --> 00:26:47,980
This is exhausting.
Gosh, I'm so tired.

421
00:26:49,450 --> 00:26:51,210
Let me take this and recharge a bit.

422
00:26:53,220 --> 00:26:54,220
All right.

423
00:26:57,120 --> 00:26:58,250
What's this?

424
00:27:03,030 --> 00:27:04,230
A necklace?

425
00:27:09,030 --> 00:27:10,030
Who's there?

426
00:27:12,370 --> 00:27:13,640
Goodness, Ms. Kang.

427
00:27:15,010 --> 00:27:16,110
What are you doing here?

428
00:27:16,640 --> 00:27:18,480
The lights were on,
so I thought you were working late.

429
00:27:18,980 --> 00:27:20,210
It must be Team Leader Kang's.

430
00:27:20,980 --> 00:27:22,080
I should return it to her.

431
00:27:24,280 --> 00:27:25,280
Manager Park.

432
00:27:25,280 --> 00:27:26,420
- Hey.
- Hello.

433
00:27:26,420 --> 00:27:28,320
Chief Cha, hello.

434
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:30,490
- Where are you headed?
- To the Design Team.

435
00:27:30,550 --> 00:27:31,550
Really? So am I.

436
00:27:31,790 --> 00:27:33,290
- Really?
- Yes.

437
00:27:34,520 --> 00:27:36,230
Well, in that case...

438
00:27:38,900 --> 00:27:41,530
Could you give this
to Ms. Kang for me?

439
00:27:41,830 --> 00:27:42,830
What's this?

440
00:27:43,100 --> 00:27:45,300
She dropped it in my office.

441
00:27:45,940 --> 00:27:46,940
Oh, dear.

442
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:49,410
All right. I'll do that.

443
00:27:50,170 --> 00:27:52,840
- Thank you so much.
- Don't mention it.

444
00:27:53,140 --> 00:27:54,610
Please make sure she gets this.

445
00:27:55,510 --> 00:27:56,910
- Good luck.
- Thanks.

446
00:28:00,520 --> 00:28:01,520
Right.

447
00:28:18,500 --> 00:28:20,570
(Cheongma)

448
00:28:21,100 --> 00:28:22,110
Hello.

449
00:28:31,880 --> 00:28:32,920
Where are you headed?

450
00:28:33,750 --> 00:28:35,120
To the Design Team.

451
00:28:36,320 --> 00:28:38,020
Is there something you need
from our team?

452
00:28:38,390 --> 00:28:40,120
I heard the new product samples
are ready.

453
00:28:41,220 --> 00:28:42,230
I see.

454
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:47,860
By the way,
what's that in your hand?

455
00:28:49,370 --> 00:28:52,340
This?
This is Team Leader Kang's necklace.

456
00:28:53,170 --> 00:28:54,170
What?

457
00:28:55,810 --> 00:28:56,910
Why are you so surprised?

458
00:28:58,270 --> 00:28:59,280
It's just...

459
00:28:59,940 --> 00:29:02,480
How come you have it, Chief Cha?

460
00:29:03,910 --> 00:29:06,780
It seems she dropped it
in Manager Park's office.

461
00:29:06,950 --> 00:29:08,080
He asked me to return it to her.

462
00:29:09,590 --> 00:29:10,650
I see.

463
00:29:13,660 --> 00:29:15,460
Here. This is us.

464
00:29:22,370 --> 00:29:23,800
Chief Cha, wait.

465
00:29:25,440 --> 00:29:26,440
Yes?

466
00:29:28,270 --> 00:29:30,870
Can we talk for a moment?

467
00:29:31,410 --> 00:29:32,510
(Design Team)

468
00:29:32,580 --> 00:29:33,580
Right now?

469
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:35,250
Yes.

470
00:29:48,530 --> 00:29:49,530
What's this about?

471
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:56,530
Look, Ms. Ko...

472
00:29:58,370 --> 00:30:00,940
Seok Jin, that necklace...

473
00:30:00,940 --> 00:30:02,110
It's actually mine.

474
00:30:05,640 --> 00:30:06,810
This necklace is yours?

475
00:30:08,140 --> 00:30:11,050
Yes, so please give it to me.

476
00:30:13,320 --> 00:30:14,380
Wait a minute.

477
00:30:21,420 --> 00:30:24,130
But why was this necklace
in Manager Park's office?

478
00:30:29,130 --> 00:30:30,700
That's because...

479
00:30:32,170 --> 00:30:33,800
I was in Manager Park's office.

480
00:30:34,540 --> 00:30:36,710
I must've dropped it
while running an errand.

481
00:30:39,110 --> 00:30:41,910
Then why was he so sure
it was Team Leader Kang's?

482
00:30:43,350 --> 00:30:44,750
He could've thought it was yours.

483
00:30:46,020 --> 00:30:48,050
Well, I have no idea why he didn't.

484
00:30:48,850 --> 00:30:49,850
Tell me the truth.

485
00:30:51,350 --> 00:30:52,360
About what?

486
00:30:53,260 --> 00:30:55,490
You've been acting suspiciously
since we were in the elevator.

487
00:30:56,390 --> 00:30:57,560
You're hiding something, aren't you?

488
00:30:58,530 --> 00:30:59,660
No, I'm not hiding anything.

489
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:04,300
You've really changed a lot.

490
00:31:07,040 --> 00:31:09,170
You're nothing like
the Ko Eun Seol I remember.

491
00:31:11,570 --> 00:31:12,580
What?

492
00:31:16,180 --> 00:31:17,280
Does going to prison...

493
00:31:19,080 --> 00:31:20,280
make everyone change like you?

494
00:31:25,260 --> 00:31:28,190
So give it to me straight
before I jump to conclusions.

495
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:35,970
Ko Eun Seol.

496
00:31:37,630 --> 00:31:39,370
What's going on here?

497
00:31:47,640 --> 00:31:49,580
What do you two think you're doing?

498
00:32:28,990 --> 00:32:32,690
(A Trap Called Desire)

499
00:32:32,820 --> 00:32:35,590
It's a bit worrying
that you don't seem that driven.

500
00:32:35,860 --> 00:32:38,460
Why is
the Design Team's new hire here?

501
00:32:38,560 --> 00:32:40,430
You used to listen to me
unconditionally.

502
00:32:40,460 --> 00:32:41,730
What's gotten into you lately?

503
00:32:41,730 --> 00:32:44,600
You aren't trying to marry Hae Ra
just for her background, right?

504
00:32:44,770 --> 00:32:46,970
What if Teun Teun's mom sees you?

505
00:32:47,040 --> 00:32:49,770
Don't go stirring up feelings
in that woman for no reason.

506
00:32:50,010 --> 00:32:51,970
I can't let you face
this danger alone.

507
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:54,580
Leave it to me. I have a plan.

508
00:32:54,580 --> 00:32:57,050
- Seok Jin.
- Hae Ra, don't you trust me?

509
00:32:57,180 --> 00:32:58,880
What are you so scared of?

510
00:32:58,980 --> 00:33:00,650
The way you're behaving...

511
00:33:00,650 --> 00:33:02,920
makes it feel like
I might have a shot.

512
00:33:03,050 --> 00:33:06,490
How cute. I just wanted
to see it for myself at least once.

513
00:33:07,090 --> 00:33:09,090
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
